From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:03:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] VizsnInstance::getAudio: end the read with the text

VizsnInstance::getAudio said it filled every read, also past the end of
the text, so the mixer never saw the voice end: a looping Vizsn never
looped and played silence instead. The read now stops at the end of the
text (the rest of the block is still zeroed), as other sources' reads do,
and the mixer seeks to the loop point. Test: vizsn_loops.
---
 src/audiosource/vizsn/soloud_vizsn.cpp | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/vizsn/soloud_vizsn.cpp b/src/audiosource/vizsn/soloud_vizsn.cpp
index 665b6a8..a71827c 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/vizsn/soloud_vizsn.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/vizsn/soloud_vizsn.cpp
@@ -268,10 +268,11 @@ namespace SoLoud
 
 			if (*mS == P_END)
 			{
-				// Past the text the block is silent.
-				for (; idx < aSamplesToRead; idx++)
-					aBuffer[idx] = 0;
-				break;
+				// Past the text the block is silent, and the read ends
+				// there, so that the mixer sees the end and loops.
+				for (unsigned int k = idx; k < aSamplesToRead; k++)
+					aBuffer[k] = 0;
+				return idx;
 			}
 
 			setphone(&mBank1, mS[1], mPitch);//pitch+=50);  -- RAISE SOUND
